.TH INGOT 1 "2026-04-06" "ingot 1.0.0" "Ingot Manual"
.SH NAME
ingot \- embedded database C code generator with compile-time perfect hashing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ingot
.B \-\-model
.I path
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-target
.IR target ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-events ]
.RB [ \-v ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ingot
reads a TOML data model specification and generates optimized C99 code for
key-value storage on resource-constrained embedded systems.
All data structures are statically allocated.
Key lookup is O(1) via minimal perfect hashing using the CHM algorithm with
Jenkins lookup3 hash.
.PP
The generated code includes:
.IP \(bu 2
Type-dispatch get/set API (\fBdm.h\fR/\fBdm.c\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Per-type storage modules (boolean bitfields, integer arrays, string buffers)
.IP \(bu 2
Perfect hash tables with Jenkins hash function
.IP \(bu 2
Key definitions as \fB#define\fR constants with encoded 32-bit values
.IP \(bu 2
Optional named helper getters/setters
.IP \(bu 2
Optional persistence (binary save/load with magic number validation)
.IP \(bu 2
Optional event callbacks on value change
.IP \(bu 2
Unity test suite with CMakeLists.txt
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-model " " path
Path to the TOML data model specification file.
Required.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " " dir
Output directory for generated C code.
Created if it does not exist.
Default: \fBgenerated/\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-target " " target
Target platform for code generation.
Affects mutex type, alignment, and pointer width.
Default: \fBlinux64\fR.
.RS
.TP
.B stm32
32-bit ARM STM32 microcontrollers.
Bare-metal (no mutex), 4-byte alignment.
.TP
.B esp\-xtensa
ESP32 Xtensa-based SoCs.
FreeRTOS semaphore mutex.
.TP
.B esp\-riscv
ESP32 RISC-V based SoCs.
FreeRTOS semaphore mutex.
.TP
.B mcu8bit
8-bit microcontrollers.
Bare-metal (no mutex), 1-byte alignment, 16-bit pointers.
.TP
.B linux64
64-bit Linux systems.
pthread mutex with PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-no\-events
Disable event callback generation.
When set, \fBDataModel_Initialize()\fR takes no arguments and no callback
is fired after successful set operations.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-vv\fR, \fB\-vvv
Increase verbosity.
One \fB-v\fR enables info-level output, two enables debug, three enables
trace.
Default log level is warnings only.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error: invalid model, validation failure, I/O error, or template rendering
failure.
A diagnostic message is printed to stderr.
.SH DATA MODEL FORMAT
The input is a TOML file with three sections:
.PP
.B [meta]
\- Namespace metadata (id, version, optional doc).
.PP
.B [enums.\fIname\fB]
\- Named enum definitions with integer values and optional per-variant
overrides.
.PP
.B [[classes]]
\- Key groups.
Each class contains
.B [[classes.keys]]
entries with attributes: type, default, defaults, enum, max_size,
read_only, thread_safe, persistent, event, helpers, unit, doc.
.PP
Supported data types: bool, uint8, int8, uint16, int16, uint32, int32,
string, binary.
String and binary types require the
.B max_size
attribute.
.PP
See
.I examples/
in the source distribution for complete examples.
.SH GENERATED FILES
.TS
l l.
dm.h / dm.c	Main API with type-dispatch get/set
dm_key.h	Key bitfield union, type enum, query macros
key_definitions.h	#define per key with encoded 32-bit value
dm_namespace_definitions.h	Namespace ID constant
boolean_storage.h/.c	Bitfield-packed boolean storage
integer_storage.h/.c	Per-type integer storage arrays
string_storage.h/.c	Read-only and read-write string storage
persistence_storage.h/.c	Binary save/load for persistent keys
jenkins_hash.h/.c	Jenkins lookup3 hash function
dm_helpers.h/.c	Named getter/setter convenience functions
dm_full.yaml	Resolved model manifest (YAML)
test_dm.c	Unity test suite
CMakeLists.txt	CMake build configuration for tests
.TE
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate C code for a data model targeting STM32:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ingot --model device.toml --output src/dm/ --target stm32
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate without event callbacks (smaller code):
.PP
.RS
.nf
ingot --model device.toml --output src/dm/ --no-events
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verbose generation for debugging:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ingot --model device.toml -vv
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B ingot
looks for its Tera template files in a
.I templates/
directory relative to the executable, then relative to the current working
directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full user guide is available at
.I docs/user\-guide.md
in the source distribution.
